                           Building PROVOX Version 7.0
        
        The PROVOX7 program is written in the assembly language A86 for 
        Intel 80x86 processors. The shareware assembler by Eric Isaacson 
        for this language is also called A86. The A86 assembly step and 
        the linking step with Borland TLINK are shown below.
        
        d:\provox7> a86 *.a
        Environment 86=+os
        A86 macro assembler, V3.22 Copyright 1990 Eric Isaacson
        Sources:
        0PREFACE.A 1I5CODE.A 2I8CODE.A 3I9CODE.A
        4I9JUMPS.A 5OTHERS.A 6I16CODE.A 7I22CODE.A
        8I47CODE.A 9PROVOX7.A
        Object: PROVOX7.OBJ
        
        d:\provox7> tlink -k provox7
        Turbo Link Version 7.00 Copyright (c) 1987, 1994 Borland International
        
        d:\provox7>
        
        The PV7 program is written in C++ and is entirely contained in a 
        single file called pv7.cpp. It is compiled with Borland C++ 
        Version 4.51. The object program must be linked with DTC.LIB from 
        RC Systems to form the executable program. Those steps are shown 
        below.
        
        d:\provox7> bcc -Id:\bc45\include -Ld:\bc45\lib pv7 dtc.lib
        
        Borland C++ 4.51 Copyright (c) 1987, 1994 Borland International
        pv7.cpp:
        
        Turbo Link Version 7.00 Copyright (c) 1987, 1994 Borland International
        
        d:\provox7>
        
        The above procedures produce the executable programs PROVOX7.EXE 
        and PV7.EXE. Recommendations for freeware or shareware tools to 
        replace the commercial linker and compiler used to build this 
        software are welcome.
        
